drawn by leave, but Senator Birmingham has now moved his motion. Simon Birmingham There is, potentially, a long list of legislation to be dealt with today. I won't detain the chamber. I make the point that the opposition is proposing to include a piece of government legislation. It's legislation that is viewed by industry and others as being important, that has progressed through the House and that has been awaiting progress through the Senate. In our view, in terms of ensuring economic certainty, progress and energy certainty in this country, this is an important bill to consider. That is why we are moving for its inclusion. I would urge the government to support their own legislation by having this bill included. Sue Lines The question is that the motion as moved by Senator Birmingham be agreed to.","result":"affirmative","slug":"division-federal-senate-8842","source_url":"https://theyvoteforyou.org.au/divisions/senate/2024-03-27/6"}
